<Project>
  <!--
    The packaged bridge and the supported Cheat Engine host are Windows x64 only. An AnyCPU library (or one with an
    unset PlatformTarget) is valid because the x64 host selects the process architecture; every explicit architecture
    other than x64 is incompatible before compilation starts.
  -->
  <Target Name="CheatEngineSdkRequireX64Platform"
          BeforeTargets="BeforeBuild"
          Condition="'$(PlatformTarget)' != '' and '$(PlatformTarget)' != 'AnyCPU' and '$(PlatformTarget)' != 'x64'">
    <Error Code="CESDK9101"
           Text="$(MSBuildProjectName) targets PlatformTarget=$(PlatformTarget). Cheat Engine and the packaged Lua protection bridge support Windows x64 only: set &lt;PlatformTarget&gt;x64&lt;/PlatformTarget&gt;, set &lt;PlatformTarget&gt;AnyCPU&lt;/PlatformTarget&gt;, or leave PlatformTarget unset."/>
  </Target>

  <!--
    A NativeAOT plugin DLL is not a supported CheatEngine.SDK profile (audit F02): Cheat Engine unloads plugins with
    FreeLibrary, and .NET does not support unloading a NativeAOT library
    (https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/core/deploying/native-aot/libraries). CheatEngine.SDK plugins load through the
    managed hostfxr profile, as a framework-dependent plugin folder. A direct consumer library that sets PublishAot
    (with or without NativeLib) therefore gets a warning at build time, before anything is published. An executable
    (Exe or WinExe) is a different artefact and is not warned: publishing an AOT-compatible tool is fine. The warning is
    suppressible with NoWarn (MSBuild demotes it to a message); see
    https://github.com/CheatEngineNet/CheatEngine.SDK/blob/main/libs/CheatEngine.SDK.Abi/README.md.
  -->
  <Target Name="CheatEngineSdkWarnNativeAotPluginProfile"
          BeforeTargets="BeforeBuild"
          Condition="'$(PublishAot)' == 'true' and '$(OutputType)' != 'Exe' and '$(OutputType)' != 'WinExe'">
    <Warning Code="CESDK9102"
             HelpLink="https://github.com/CheatEngineNet/CheatEngine.SDK/blob/main/analyzers/docs/CESDK9102.md"
             Text="$(MSBuildProjectName) sets PublishAot=true (NativeLib=$(NativeLib)) on a library that references CheatEngine.SDK directly. Cheat Engine unloads plugins with FreeLibrary, which .NET does not support for NativeAOT libraries; CheatEngine.SDK plugins load through the managed hostfxr profile only, as a framework-dependent plugin folder. Remove PublishAot from the plugin, or add CESDK9102 to NoWarn if this library is not a Cheat Engine plugin."/>
  </Target>
</Project>
